1
00:00:03,525 --> 00:00:05,483
♪♪♪

2
00:00:11,315 --> 00:00:12,708
[engine turns off]

3
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,716
You're wasting time with me.

4
00:00:20,803 --> 00:00:22,500
You should be looking
for those hooligans

5
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:23,545
he had hanging around.

6
00:00:23,632 --> 00:00:25,242
Mr. Liu.
He owns the building

7
00:00:25,329 --> 00:00:27,723
that has the import export
business on the first floor.

8
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:29,638
Patrick Jane

9
00:00:29,725 --> 00:00:33,076
I rented him the upstairs
because he seemed reliable.

10
00:00:33,163 --> 00:00:35,644
But he wasn't.
You find those kids.

11
00:00:35,731 --> 00:00:37,559
I don't need
these kind of problems.

12
00:00:37,646 --> 00:00:40,127
What are you
so scared about?

13
00:00:40,214 --> 00:00:42,042
Scared about losing money,
that's what.

14
00:00:42,129 --> 00:00:43,260
Mm.

15
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:45,175
I need to get back to work.

16
00:00:47,003 --> 00:00:48,048
Me, too.

17
00:00:48,135 --> 00:00:50,398
[camera shutter clicks]

18
00:00:50,485 --> 00:00:52,095
[Patrick]
'Morning, Lisbon.'

19
00:00:52,182 --> 00:00:53,488
'What do we have here?'

20
00:00:53,575 --> 00:00:56,056
[Lisbon]
'Somebody named Theissens.'

21
00:00:56,143 --> 00:01:00,190
He doesn't have a wallet on him,
but I'm not thinking robbery.

22
00:01:00,277 --> 00:01:03,193
Looks like
a puritan tailor shop.

23
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,022
Helpful. That's it?
That's all you're gonna say?

24
00:01:06,109 --> 00:01:08,546
Till I think of something
useful to say, yes.

25
00:01:10,244 --> 00:01:12,898
No murder weapon, but there was
this... in his mouth.

26
00:01:12,985 --> 00:01:14,291
In his mouth?

27
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:15,988
This is definitely not
a robbery.

28
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:18,469
- Crime of passion?
- Or a message.

29
00:01:18,556 --> 00:01:20,776
Let's keep the feather
out of any public statements.

30
00:01:20,863 --> 00:01:22,691
It could be useful
identifying the killer.

31
00:01:22,778 --> 00:01:23,909
A feather?

32
00:01:23,996 --> 00:01:26,303
Now we're getting somewhere.

33
00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:28,218
Find out
where this came from.

34
00:01:28,305 --> 00:01:30,220
Came from his mouth.

35
00:01:30,307 --> 00:01:34,137
Yes, uh, before
it was in his... mouth.

36
00:01:34,224 --> 00:01:36,835
Maybe the killer brought it in?
Or the killers?

37
00:01:36,922 --> 00:01:38,098
Could be
this is gang-related.

38
00:01:38,185 --> 00:01:39,577
A golden feather?

39
00:01:39,664 --> 00:01:42,145
It's a little camp for
gangsters, don't you think?

40
00:01:42,232 --> 00:01:44,365
I think it has
something to do with dresses.

41
00:01:46,193 --> 00:01:47,324
Dresses..

42
00:01:53,461 --> 00:01:56,681
Hmm.
Interesting.

43
00:01:56,768 --> 00:01:58,596
[click]

44
00:02:03,514 --> 00:02:05,386
Ah, secret room.

45
00:02:06,604 --> 00:02:07,910
[door bangs]

46
00:02:11,087 --> 00:02:12,175
Ooh-la-la!

47
00:02:21,402 --> 00:02:22,838
Et voila!

48
00:02:22,925 --> 00:02:24,144
The murder weapon.

49
00:02:30,106 --> 00:02:32,021
[theme music

50
00:02:40,203 --> 00:02:42,118
[telephone ringing]

51
00:02:42,205 --> 00:02:45,600
So Wyck Theissens was a clothing
designer in New York and Paris.

52
00:02:45,687 --> 00:02:47,819
Real high-end stuff.
Cutting edge. Very successful.

53
00:02:47,906 --> 00:02:50,213
Then about three years ago,
it all went bad.

54
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,215
Bad how?

55
00:02:52,302 --> 00:02:53,216
Bad like this.

56
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:57,612
You're... you're not taping
this, are you?

57
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:59,483
[Man]
'No. We're just warming up.'

58
00:02:59,570 --> 00:03:00,789
'Uh, the fashion world is...'

59
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:03,008
'Yeah, uh, the fashion world'

60
00:03:03,095 --> 00:03:07,535
'is pond scum and monsters.
That's all it is. They're...'

61
00:03:07,622 --> 00:03:11,495
'It's crawling lickspittle
pond scum like you, and...'

62
00:03:11,582 --> 00:03:15,630
'warty, great monsters
like Guy Duval.'

63
00:03:15,717 --> 00:03:17,197
Who's Duval?

64
00:03:17,284 --> 00:03:19,982
He's a French C.E.O.
Of a luxury goods conglomerate.

65
00:03:20,069 --> 00:03:22,593
Holdings are mostly jewelry,
watches, perfume, fashion.

66
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,595
He was backing Theissens'
clothing line, but obviously,

67
00:03:24,682 --> 00:03:26,641
he fired him
after that video came out.

68
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:28,991
And I'm part of it all.

69
00:03:29,078 --> 00:03:32,473
Look at me.

70
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,345
What an ugly creep I am.

71
00:03:35,432 --> 00:03:37,608
[glass shatters]

72
00:03:37,695 --> 00:03:38,957
That's about two years ago.

73
00:03:39,044 --> 00:03:40,481
Theissens had a breakdown
and disappeared.

74
00:03:40,568 --> 00:03:42,222
What was he doing here?

75
00:03:42,309 --> 00:03:44,267
Not much, according
to the paperwork I got.

76
00:03:44,354 --> 00:03:45,703
Cobbled together
bits of tailoring

77
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:47,531
for clothing shops around town.
That's it.

78
00:03:47,618 --> 00:03:49,141
What about the stuff
Jane found?

79
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,752
I don't know.

80
00:03:50,839 --> 00:03:53,276
The materials for these dresses
alone comes to $250,000.

81
00:03:53,363 --> 00:03:54,495
- Really?
- Yeah.

82
00:03:54,582 --> 00:03:56,018
Cashmere? Watered silk?
Vicuna?

83
00:03:56,105 --> 00:03:59,326
You know what this stuff
prices out per yard?

84
00:03:59,413 --> 00:04:01,371
What about the murder weapon?
We get prints?

85
00:04:01,458 --> 00:04:02,894
Yeah, but nothing
that matches anything

86
00:04:02,981 --> 00:04:04,940
in the criminal database
or D.M.V.

87
00:04:05,027 --> 00:04:07,464
Look into his financials,
see if you can find anything.

88
00:04:07,551 --> 00:04:09,074
Yeah, you got it.

89
00:04:12,643 --> 00:04:14,297
What?

90
00:04:14,384 --> 00:04:15,603
Fashion? Really?

91
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:17,692
Come on. Beautiful women
in nice clothes?

92
00:04:17,779 --> 00:04:18,910
What's not to like?

93
00:04:24,394 --> 00:04:27,528
Who would wanna murder
a washed-up fashion designer?

94
00:04:27,615 --> 00:04:28,790
Hmm.

95
00:04:28,877 --> 00:04:30,574
Why would
a washed-up fashion designer

96
00:04:30,661 --> 00:04:32,576
hide a quarter-million dollars
in couture dresses

97
00:04:32,663 --> 00:04:34,317
in a loft in Oakland?

98
00:04:34,404 --> 00:04:37,668
Boss, uh, one of the cops from
the crime scene just called in.

99
00:04:37,755 --> 00:04:40,715
Some kids showed up at the loft,
said they worked for Theissens.

100
00:04:40,802 --> 00:04:42,760
- Have the cops bring them in.
- Will do.

101
00:04:42,847 --> 00:04:45,546
No. Let's go to them.
Seeing them in their own element

102
00:04:45,633 --> 00:04:47,199
will be more revealing.

103
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,724
- You just like the loft.
- I do. It's very nice.

104
00:04:49,811 --> 00:04:51,508
- I've to be back after lunch.
- Oh?

105
00:04:51,595 --> 00:04:53,075
Management meeting.

106
00:04:53,162 --> 00:04:56,513
That Wainwright has too much
time on his hands.

107
00:05:01,736 --> 00:05:03,607
Agent Wainwright?
Patrick Jane

108
00:05:03,694 --> 00:05:05,914
Hi, yeah. I just wanted
to let you know

109
00:05:06,001 --> 00:05:08,308
that Agent Lisbon is needed
urgently in the field

110
00:05:08,395 --> 00:05:10,135
and as important
as your seminar is

111
00:05:10,222 --> 00:05:13,138
she's not gonna be able
to attend.

112
00:05:13,225 --> 00:05:15,489
Okay. Thank you. Bye-bye.

113
00:05:15,576 --> 00:05:16,881
He said it's fine.

114
00:05:16,968 --> 00:05:18,579
See? Simple as that.

115
00:05:18,666 --> 00:05:20,015
Mm. Thanks.

116
00:05:20,102 --> 00:05:22,539
Did it ever occur to you
that I might actually

117
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:24,062
want to go to the meeting?

118
00:05:24,149 --> 00:05:25,803
No, it didn't. Do you?

119
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:28,066
No. But it's the principle.

120
00:05:32,593 --> 00:05:34,377
Sorry about that.

121
00:05:34,464 --> 00:05:37,424
So, you were saying?

122
00:05:37,511 --> 00:05:39,687
I wanted to let you know
as a courtesy

123
00:05:39,774 --> 00:05:41,297
I'm still working
the Panzer murder.

124
00:05:41,384 --> 00:05:43,517
The San Joaquin killer case
was solved.

125
00:05:43,604 --> 00:05:45,562
James Panzer was killed
by Tom Maier

126
00:05:45,649 --> 00:05:47,434
the father
of the first victim.

127
00:05:47,521 --> 00:05:49,784
I'm not certain about that.

128
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:51,263
Well, there was
conclusive evidence.

129
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:52,787
There was the murder weapon

130
00:05:52,874 --> 00:05:54,354
Panzer's blood
on Maier's clothing

131
00:05:54,441 --> 00:05:57,008
not to mention
the confession Maier wrote

132
00:05:57,095 --> 00:05:58,140
before killing himself.

133
00:05:58,227 --> 00:05:59,663
Right. Odd, don't you think?

134
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:02,492
Why'd he go to such lengths
to make it look like

135
00:06:02,579 --> 00:06:05,016
Red John was the killer?
It doesn't make any sense.

136
00:06:05,103 --> 00:06:08,542
And why would he send CBI
a video of me?

137
00:06:11,022 --> 00:06:15,723
Who can fathom the mind
of a desperate man?

138
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:18,769
I'm gonna need all the
department files on Red John.

139
00:06:18,856 --> 00:06:20,162
Of course.

140
00:06:20,249 --> 00:06:22,077
Yeah, whatever
the bureau needs

141
00:06:22,164 --> 00:06:25,036
we are always happy
to be of assistance.

142
00:06:27,082 --> 00:06:29,127
Where were you three
last night?

143
00:06:29,214 --> 00:06:31,913
- Jail.
- Why?

144
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,524
We were at the occupied
demonstration downtown.

145
00:06:34,611 --> 00:06:37,309
Cops said we had to clear the
plaza, then arrested everybody.

146
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,573
We didn't get out
until about an hour ago.

147
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,357
What's your connection
to Wyck Theissens?

148
00:06:41,444 --> 00:06:43,664
We were working with him
on his next collection.

149
00:06:43,751 --> 00:06:45,709
He found us
at the fashion institute.

150
00:06:45,796 --> 00:06:47,276
He wanted to work with people

151
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:49,583
that were not yet tainted
by the industry.

152
00:06:49,670 --> 00:06:52,324
Yeah. Yeah, that's right.

153
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:54,370
I mean, he'd been screwed over
once before.

154
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:55,893
Wasn't gonna make
that mistake again.

155
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,982
Everybody wanted to know
what he was doing..

156
00:06:58,069 --> 00:07:00,115
calling, nosing around.

157
00:07:00,202 --> 00:07:02,204
That why he built
the secret room?

158
00:07:02,291 --> 00:07:04,336
So no one could see the clothes?

159
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:07,296
Where'd the money come from
for all this?

160
00:07:07,383 --> 00:07:09,864
We made dresses
for the guy downstairs

161
00:07:09,951 --> 00:07:11,866
for him to send back to Asia.

162
00:07:11,953 --> 00:07:13,563
Knockoffs of haute couture.

163
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:15,739
Mr. Liu?
With the import-export business?

164
00:07:15,826 --> 00:07:17,828
Yeah. It was good training.

165
00:07:17,915 --> 00:07:20,918
Sure. Okay. Any idea why Mr. Liu
would name you three

166
00:07:21,005 --> 00:07:23,051
as the most likely suspects?

167
00:07:23,138 --> 00:07:24,313
[chuckles]
No.

168
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,097
He's just pissed
'cause we weren't gonna

169
00:07:26,184 --> 00:07:27,838
make any more knockoffs
for him.

170
00:07:27,925 --> 00:07:29,449
Yeah, once the collection
was finished

171
00:07:29,536 --> 00:07:31,233
Wyck told him
that we were done.

172
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,235
And when were you gonna
show this collection?

173
00:07:33,322 --> 00:07:34,802
Next week.

174
00:07:34,889 --> 00:07:37,935
Everyone in the fashion world
was coming out for it.

175
00:07:38,022 --> 00:07:39,763
And Theissens
was okay with that?

176
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:41,983
He didn't have
any bad feelings?

177
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:44,899
He made his peace with
the business aspects, you know?

178
00:07:44,986 --> 00:07:47,075
Said it was a necessary evil.

179
00:07:47,162 --> 00:07:49,947
Said if you wanna get
your vision to the world..

180
00:07:50,034 --> 00:07:51,993
...you gotta work
with the devil.

181
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,690
Even Guy Duval.

182
00:07:53,777 --> 00:07:55,344
What about Guy Duval?

183
00:07:55,431 --> 00:07:58,913
He's this big
corporate fashion guy.

184
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,523
And, um, two nights ago

185
00:08:00,610 --> 00:08:03,613
after this dinner
at a hotel in San Francisco

186
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:07,312
Wyck and him were, like,
hugely arguing.

187
00:08:07,399 --> 00:08:09,793
[cell phone rings]

188
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:12,579
- Hey, boss. What's up?
- I need you to talk to Liu

189
00:08:12,666 --> 00:08:15,103
about paying Theissens
to knock off couture dresses

190
00:08:15,190 --> 00:08:16,278
for the Asian market.

191
00:08:16,365 --> 00:08:18,280
Liu? He's not there?

192
00:08:18,367 --> 00:08:21,022
[Lisbon]
'I'm just leaving his warehouse
now and his employees said'

193
00:08:21,109 --> 00:08:23,590
that he went to speak to you
at the CBI.

194
00:08:23,677 --> 00:08:25,113
Well, somebody's lying.
He's not here.

195
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,115
'Alright.
We need to find Liu.'

196
00:08:27,202 --> 00:08:30,031
We're headed to talk
to Duval now. Keep in touch.

197
00:08:30,118 --> 00:08:32,555
Okay. Will do.

198
00:08:36,690 --> 00:08:39,519
I'm Mr. Duval's assistant.
Can I help you?

199
00:08:39,606 --> 00:08:42,391
Yes, I need to speak with your
boss. It's police business.

200
00:08:42,478 --> 00:08:46,482
I'm sorry. Mr. Duval
is not available at the moment.

201
00:08:46,569 --> 00:08:47,831
When will he be available?

202
00:08:49,964 --> 00:08:53,010
[assistant]
'Let me set something up.
When's a good time for you?'

203
00:08:53,097 --> 00:08:54,446
[cell phone rings]

204
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:58,102
Would you excuse me?
What's up?

205
00:08:58,189 --> 00:09:01,149
[Rigsby]
'Hey, boss. Just got off
the phone with Oakland P.D.

206
00:09:01,236 --> 00:09:03,412
- Liu's in the wind.
- Already? How?

207
00:09:03,499 --> 00:09:05,719
Cops went to his residence.
Liu was already gone.

208
00:09:05,806 --> 00:09:08,460
Neighbors say three Asian guys
came and he left with them.

209
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,027
Did we get a license plate?

210
00:09:10,114 --> 00:09:12,203
No, but we're working
on his phone now.

211
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:13,378
Alright. Keep in touch.

212
00:09:13,465 --> 00:09:16,643
Jane and I are
headed back there now.

213
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:19,733
Could you tell your boss
to call me as soon as possible?

214
00:09:21,256 --> 00:09:24,259
[Lisbon]
'Jane, where are you?'

215
00:09:24,346 --> 00:09:26,130
'Jane?'

216
00:09:26,217 --> 00:09:28,132
'Jane! Where are you?'

217
00:09:28,219 --> 00:09:30,657
[dance music playing]

218
00:09:33,921 --> 00:09:35,313
Next.

219
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,882
Next.

220
00:09:38,969 --> 00:09:42,146
Guy Duval, yes?

221
00:09:42,233 --> 00:09:44,584
GheeDuval.
Ah.

222
00:09:44,671 --> 00:09:46,411
The room is closed
to the public.

223
00:09:46,498 --> 00:09:48,196
Mr. Duval, I am so,
so sorry.

224
00:09:48,283 --> 00:09:51,199
Agent Lisbon,
meet GheeDuval.

225
00:09:51,286 --> 00:09:53,505
Hey, Vato,
who invited you to sit?

226
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:56,770
- And you are?
- I'm Junior Acosta.

227
00:09:56,857 --> 00:09:59,511
I sense that's supposed
to mean something to me.

228
00:10:04,386 --> 00:10:06,954
Junior Acosta's
a very important man.

229
00:10:07,041 --> 00:10:10,131
He puts together
all my shows and parties.

230
00:10:10,218 --> 00:10:11,567
What is this about?

231
00:10:11,654 --> 00:10:13,569
I'm Agent Lisbon
with the CBI

232
00:10:13,656 --> 00:10:16,006
and this is my colleague,
Patrick Jane

233
00:10:16,093 --> 00:10:18,705
We need to ask you some
questions about Wyck Theissens.

234
00:10:18,792 --> 00:10:20,707
What about him?

235
00:10:20,794 --> 00:10:22,186
Theissens is dead.

236
00:10:24,101 --> 00:10:25,712
Oh, my God.

237
00:10:25,799 --> 00:10:28,715
What were you two arguing about
at dinner the other night?

238
00:10:28,802 --> 00:10:30,891
'Was it about
his new clothing line?'

239
00:10:30,978 --> 00:10:33,676
I haven't even seen the line.

240
00:10:33,763 --> 00:10:35,722
He wouldn't let anyone see it.

241
00:10:35,809 --> 00:10:37,941
You're about to buy
a line of clothing

242
00:10:38,028 --> 00:10:39,508
you hadn't been allowed
to see?

243
00:10:39,595 --> 00:10:43,294
He's a genius.
You make allowances.

244
00:10:43,381 --> 00:10:44,339
Was he killed?

245
00:10:44,426 --> 00:10:46,689
Stabbed.

246
00:10:46,776 --> 00:10:48,212
That's ugly.

247
00:10:48,299 --> 00:10:50,562
Yes. Did you make allowances
two years ago

248
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,086
when he called you a monster?

249
00:10:53,957 --> 00:10:57,744
Of course.
I took it as a compliment.

250
00:10:57,831 --> 00:11:01,225
I hope I'm a great monster.

251
00:11:01,312 --> 00:11:04,315
Wyck's career
was derailed by Wyck.

252
00:11:04,402 --> 00:11:05,752
Nobody else.

253
00:11:05,839 --> 00:11:07,710
Where were you last night,
Mr. Duval?

254
00:11:10,974 --> 00:11:12,541
Au lit..

255
00:11:12,628 --> 00:11:14,804
...avec ma femme.

256
00:11:14,891 --> 00:11:18,112
I think that means
he was in bed with his wife.

257
00:11:21,332 --> 00:11:23,334
You released Theissens' video,
didn't you?

258
00:11:24,771 --> 00:11:26,990
Yeah? So? It was news.

259
00:11:27,077 --> 00:11:29,950
So you're responsible
for derailing his career.

260
00:11:30,037 --> 00:11:32,692
No. The truth
is what it is.

261
00:11:32,779 --> 00:11:34,302
I was just a conduit.

262
00:11:34,389 --> 00:11:37,348
Yes. A conduit
is what you are.

263
00:11:37,435 --> 00:11:40,308
Why do keep
a conniving backstabber around?

264
00:11:40,395 --> 00:11:42,266
You think you can
really trust him?

265
00:11:42,353 --> 00:11:43,964
You better watch
your mouth, okay?

266
00:11:44,051 --> 00:11:46,749
Or else what? You gonna gossip
about me behind my back?

267
00:11:46,836 --> 00:11:48,795
I'll show you
what I can do, bitch.

268
00:11:48,882 --> 00:11:50,318
- Oh, okay.
- Put the knife down.

269
00:11:50,405 --> 00:11:52,842
Keep your hands
where I can see 'em.

270
00:11:52,929 --> 00:11:54,322
[clatters]

271
00:11:54,409 --> 00:11:56,585
You fashion people...
You're a very, uh..

272
00:11:56,672 --> 00:11:59,370
passionate lot,
aren't you?

273
00:11:59,457 --> 00:12:01,416
These are all the Red John
case files?

274
00:12:01,503 --> 00:12:03,940
Yes, sir. Four boxes
of physical evidence

275
00:12:04,027 --> 00:12:06,029
plus two hard drives
containing all photographic

276
00:12:06,116 --> 00:12:07,901
and documentary evidence.

277
00:12:07,988 --> 00:12:10,512
Okay, good. Um...

278
00:12:10,599 --> 00:12:12,383
Sign here.
FBI just called me.

279
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:14,951
They have somebody en route
coming to pick this up.

280
00:12:15,038 --> 00:12:17,824
But one more thing..
Listen to me very closely.

281
00:12:17,911 --> 00:12:19,869
This is
a highly sensitive issue.

282
00:12:19,956 --> 00:12:21,871
You're not to talk
to anybody about this.

283
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:24,613
Do you understand?
No one.

284
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:26,354
Yes, sir.
Whatever you say.

285
00:12:26,441 --> 00:12:28,660
Okay, good. If somebody comes
looking for the files

286
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:30,097
or asks where they've gone

287
00:12:30,184 --> 00:12:32,490
you're to inform me
immediately.

288
00:12:32,577 --> 00:12:34,144
I cannot stress enough
the importance

289
00:12:34,231 --> 00:12:36,973
that this remain secret.
[knock on door]

290
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:39,280
J.D.!, Who let you
out of the basement?

291
00:12:39,367 --> 00:12:40,585
Hey to you, Agent Lisbon.

292
00:12:40,672 --> 00:12:42,370
- How you been?
- Alright. How 'bout you?

293
00:12:42,457 --> 00:12:44,589
Okay, that's enough.
Thank you. Back to work.

294
00:12:47,418 --> 00:12:48,724
See ya.

295
00:12:48,811 --> 00:12:51,161
Did I call for you?

296
00:12:51,248 --> 00:12:53,642
I just wanted to apologize
for earlier..

297
00:12:53,729 --> 00:12:56,210
Jane calling to get me out
of the management meeting.

298
00:12:56,297 --> 00:12:59,866
Would it be too much to ask you
to schedule a meeting properly?

299
00:12:59,953 --> 00:13:02,607
I'm so sorry.
I didn't realize.

300
00:13:05,262 --> 00:13:06,960
How's your case going?

301
00:13:07,047 --> 00:13:08,570
It's progressing.

302
00:13:08,657 --> 00:13:11,355
We're gonna interview a suspect
if you'd like to sit in.

303
00:13:11,442 --> 00:13:13,009
Unless you're busy.

304
00:13:13,096 --> 00:13:17,318
Paperwork.
The bane of management.

305
00:13:17,405 --> 00:13:20,408
I'd like you to catch me up
when you have the time.

306
00:13:20,495 --> 00:13:22,671
Of course.
Whenever you want.

307
00:13:22,758 --> 00:13:24,020
Um..

308
00:13:24,107 --> 00:13:26,327
How about 45 minutes
in the bullpen?

309
00:13:26,414 --> 00:13:27,894
Yes, sir.

310
00:13:49,132 --> 00:13:52,657
This is a mistake. I got a
little carried away. That's all.

311
00:13:52,744 --> 00:13:55,095
You threatened my colleague
with a knife.

312
00:13:55,182 --> 00:13:58,663
Mm. And you're also a suspect
in Wyck Theissens' murder.

313
00:13:58,750 --> 00:14:01,362
Me? [chuckles]
Why would I kill him?

314
00:14:01,449 --> 00:14:03,886
Well, you ruined Theissens' life
by releasing that video.

315
00:14:03,973 --> 00:14:07,150
It's only natural that he'd
like to return the favor.

316
00:14:07,237 --> 00:14:08,848
Wh-what are you
talking about?

317
00:14:08,935 --> 00:14:11,372
I'm talking about the fact
that Duval wouldn't be happy

318
00:14:11,459 --> 00:14:14,418
to know what you and his wife
are doing behind his back.

319
00:14:14,505 --> 00:14:16,377
What?

320
00:14:16,464 --> 00:14:18,945
If Theissens learned that
you were cuckolding Duval

321
00:14:19,032 --> 00:14:22,644
then, uh, he has every reason
to reveal that fact

322
00:14:22,731 --> 00:14:24,951
which gives you
every reason to kill him.

323
00:14:25,038 --> 00:14:27,344
You can't say anything
about me and Jacqueline.

324
00:14:28,650 --> 00:14:30,565
If Duval found out,
I'd be done.

325
00:14:32,262 --> 00:14:33,655
I'd never work again.

326
00:14:33,742 --> 00:14:35,744
Where were you last night,
Mr. Acosta?

327
00:14:35,831 --> 00:14:37,398
I was at the hotel.

328
00:14:37,485 --> 00:14:39,574
Is there anybody
who can verify that?

329
00:14:43,056 --> 00:14:44,448
Okay, listen..

330
00:14:44,535 --> 00:14:46,929
...if I tell you something..

331
00:14:47,016 --> 00:14:50,019
...you wouldn't let anybody know
it was me that told you, right?

332
00:14:50,106 --> 00:14:52,065
- No.
- It depends on what it is.

333
00:14:52,152 --> 00:14:53,980
Well, I wouldn't.
She might.

334
00:14:54,067 --> 00:14:56,721
Okay, well, the thing is

335
00:14:56,808 --> 00:14:59,246
Wyck and Duval did argue
at dinner the other night.

336
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:00,421
I heard them.

337
00:15:00,508 --> 00:15:01,639
It was about Tony.

338
00:15:01,726 --> 00:15:03,163
Who's Tony?

339
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:05,600
Tony Redgrave. He's a photog.

340
00:15:05,687 --> 00:15:08,211
Everybody uses him,
but he's kind of a creep.

341
00:15:08,298 --> 00:15:09,430
Hmm.

342
00:15:09,517 --> 00:15:13,086
The thing is,
everybody uses him.

343
00:15:13,173 --> 00:15:15,001
So you can't say
I told you.

344
00:15:15,088 --> 00:15:17,133
I can't afford
to piss him off, alright?

345
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:19,744
What were they talking about?

346
00:15:19,831 --> 00:15:21,268
Wyck had brought in
some kids

347
00:15:21,355 --> 00:15:23,357
and he was pissed
that Tony was there.

348
00:15:23,444 --> 00:15:26,838
Oh, he was worried that tony
might get creepy with the kids?

349
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,579
You know, Tony--

350
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:31,060
he likes 'em young,
you know?

351
00:15:31,147 --> 00:15:32,453
Got it.

352
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:34,455
- Thank you.
- Got it.

353
00:15:39,242 --> 00:15:41,984
- So we go talk to Tony?
- Take somebody with you.

354
00:15:42,071 --> 00:15:45,379
You're not coming? This could be
your ticket out of this job.

355
00:15:45,466 --> 00:15:47,947
Ha! Wainright's coming in.
He wants to check on things.

356
00:15:48,034 --> 00:15:51,863
More managing? I mean, what--
I-- Someone's gotta do it.

357
00:15:53,996 --> 00:15:57,434
So can we bring me up to date
on the Theissens case?

358
00:15:57,521 --> 00:16:00,437
Well, sir, the alibi for
Theissens' assistants hold up.

359
00:16:00,524 --> 00:16:02,526
They were booked
and held overnight.

360
00:16:02,613 --> 00:16:03,919
But the landlord, Liu--

361
00:16:04,006 --> 00:16:05,747
the one that was selling
Theissens' knockoffs--

362
00:16:05,834 --> 00:16:07,183
he disappeared in a hurry.

363
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:09,707
And we got a court order
to track his phone.

364
00:16:09,794 --> 00:16:13,059
I can make a call, get this at
the top of their list.

365
00:16:13,146 --> 00:16:15,583
If he had a smartphone,
we might be able to

366
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:17,411
get an exact location
on the GPS.

367
00:16:17,498 --> 00:16:20,240
- Ifhe had his phone on him.
- Well, let's hope.

368
00:16:20,327 --> 00:16:22,372
And we're also looking
into Guy Duval.

369
00:16:22,459 --> 00:16:24,418
Duval was facing
a shareholder revolt.

370
00:16:24,505 --> 00:16:27,508
He had a lot pinned on making
this Theissens deal go through.

371
00:16:27,595 --> 00:16:30,076
- So if Theissens backed out--
- Then Duval would look weak

372
00:16:30,163 --> 00:16:32,078
and that would make
his position look vulnerable.

373
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:33,905
And he'd do anything to stop
that.

374
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:37,170
Jane and Van Pelt are looking
into Tony Redgrave.

375
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:39,476
And what reason would he have
for murdering Theissens?

376
00:16:39,563 --> 00:16:42,827
We don't know. It could just be
Acosta trying to throw us off.

377
00:16:42,914 --> 00:16:44,090
But Redgrave
does have priors.

378
00:16:44,177 --> 00:16:45,569
What for?
[cell phone rings]

379
00:16:45,656 --> 00:16:49,834
Providing drugs
and alcohol to minors.

380
00:16:49,921 --> 00:16:52,881
um, you, uh, you definitely have
your work cut out for you...

381
00:16:52,968 --> 00:16:56,232
so I will leave you to it.

382
00:16:56,319 --> 00:16:58,191
Excellent.

383
00:16:59,627 --> 00:17:01,281
This is Wainright.

384
00:17:01,368 --> 00:17:04,501
Hey. I just want to acknowledge
receipt of the Red John files.

385
00:17:04,588 --> 00:17:05,937
Thank you for that.

386
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:08,375
Sure. Yeah.
Anything I can do to help.

387
00:17:08,462 --> 00:17:10,681
Listen, I am assuming
we're on the same page

388
00:17:10,768 --> 00:17:13,336
but you didn't tell your people
about this, did you?

389
00:17:13,423 --> 00:17:14,946
No. I saw no need.

390
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,819
'I agree. Thanks.'

391
00:17:22,737 --> 00:17:23,868
[knocks on door]

392
00:17:23,955 --> 00:17:25,131
Baris Acar?

393
00:17:25,218 --> 00:17:27,176
Ah. Yes, ma'am.

394
00:17:27,263 --> 00:17:29,396
Susan Darcy, FBI.

395
00:17:29,483 --> 00:17:31,050
Uh, did I do
something wrong?

396
00:17:31,137 --> 00:17:33,878
No, it's nothing like that.

397
00:17:33,965 --> 00:17:36,707
I've never been interviewed
by the FBI before.

398
00:17:36,794 --> 00:17:41,321
Mr. Acar, this is
your signature, isn't it?

399
00:17:41,408 --> 00:17:42,974
Yes, ma'am, it is.

400
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,542
And this is a form telling me
that Patrick Jane

401
00:17:45,629 --> 00:17:48,676
brought a visitor here to see
the body of Timothy Carter.

402
00:17:48,763 --> 00:17:52,549
Mr. Jane shot and killed him
in a mall food court.

403
00:17:52,636 --> 00:17:53,811
Do you remember that visit?

404
00:17:53,898 --> 00:17:55,639
Uh, I sure do.

405
00:17:56,945 --> 00:17:59,643
Can you tell me about it?

406
00:17:59,730 --> 00:18:02,733
Well, it stuck in my head
because it was kind of weird.

407
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:04,344
Weird? What do you mean?

408
00:18:04,431 --> 00:18:05,867
She was blind.

409
00:18:05,954 --> 00:18:08,087
That's kind of weird, right?

410
00:18:08,174 --> 00:18:10,306
Mr. Jane's guest
was a blind woman?

411
00:18:10,393 --> 00:18:12,352
I couldn't figure out
why he brought her.

412
00:18:12,439 --> 00:18:13,701
I mean, she was blind.

413
00:18:16,834 --> 00:18:20,273
Thank you, Mr. Acar.
That's all.

414
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,796
Oh, Mr. Acar

415
00:18:21,883 --> 00:18:24,581
you do know not to speak
to anyone about this?

416
00:18:24,668 --> 00:18:25,843
Whatever you say, ma'am.

417
00:18:39,901 --> 00:18:42,599
Uh, excuse me.
Is that, uh, Tony Redgrave?

418
00:18:42,686 --> 00:18:45,994
Sasha, Sasha, Sasha..

419
00:18:46,081 --> 00:18:48,692
I'm an artist, yeah?
Not a fishmonger.

420
00:18:48,779 --> 00:18:50,651
God sakes, relax.

421
00:18:50,738 --> 00:18:53,088
How am I supposed to relax?

422
00:18:53,175 --> 00:18:54,785
Tony, you're so bloody selfish.

423
00:18:54,872 --> 00:18:57,962
Wyck is dead. He's dead.

424
00:18:58,049 --> 00:19:00,574
Circle of life, babe,
circle of life.

425
00:19:00,661 --> 00:19:03,272
Alright.
Let's try a couple more.

426
00:19:03,359 --> 00:19:05,535
That sullen, grieving look...

427
00:19:05,622 --> 00:19:07,233
I like it.

428
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,843
You Tony?

429
00:19:08,930 --> 00:19:11,411
I'm agent Van Pelt.
This is Patrick Jane

430
00:19:11,498 --> 00:19:13,891
from the California Bureau
of Investigation.

431
00:19:13,978 --> 00:19:16,416
Oh, my God. I love you.

432
00:19:16,503 --> 00:19:18,157
Take your clothes off.
Both of you.

433
00:19:20,985 --> 00:19:24,337
I'm just kidding.
look at your face.

434
00:19:24,424 --> 00:19:27,166
We're here about Wyck Theissens.

435
00:19:27,253 --> 00:19:29,559
It's really sad, right?
Really sad.

436
00:19:29,646 --> 00:19:31,605
I was about to shoot
his comeback campaign.

437
00:19:31,692 --> 00:19:34,260
What a huge bummer that was.

438
00:19:34,347 --> 00:19:37,001
Stabbed to death, right?

439
00:19:37,088 --> 00:19:40,004
What with? A knife? Razor?

440
00:19:40,091 --> 00:19:42,659
Shut up! Tony, God!

441
00:19:42,746 --> 00:19:44,531
We were like family.

442
00:19:44,618 --> 00:19:46,663
We came up together,
me and Wyck.

443
00:19:46,750 --> 00:19:49,100
I walked in every single one
of his shows.

444
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:51,407
[clicks]
Yes!

445
00:19:51,494 --> 00:19:53,017
That's it, Sasha.

446
00:19:53,104 --> 00:19:54,497
Now you're killing it.

447
00:19:54,584 --> 00:19:56,847
Where were you last night,
Mr. Redgrave?

448
00:19:56,934 --> 00:19:59,198
Oh, uh..

449
00:19:59,285 --> 00:20:01,069
Let's see..

450
00:20:01,156 --> 00:20:04,464
I was... downstairs..

451
00:20:04,551 --> 00:20:08,424
at the pool for a little bit.
Then some drinks at the bar

452
00:20:08,511 --> 00:20:10,948
then dinner,
then we came up here.

453
00:20:11,035 --> 00:20:14,038
Who's "we"?

454
00:20:14,125 --> 00:20:16,824
I don't know. Everyone.

455
00:20:16,911 --> 00:20:19,870
You came up here for a bit,
didn't you, darling?

456
00:20:19,957 --> 00:20:22,046
Yes, you were.
Chin up.

457
00:20:22,133 --> 00:20:26,181
It's quite the act, this, uh,
wide-eyed man-child bit.

458
00:20:26,268 --> 00:20:30,664
Nobody ever calls you
on it, do they?

459
00:20:30,751 --> 00:20:33,275
I'm just really lucky,
you know?

460
00:20:33,362 --> 00:20:37,148
It's just about living
in the moment. Having some fun.

461
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:40,761
Ah, yes. The joys
of living in the moment.

462
00:20:40,848 --> 00:20:42,937
All fun and games
till someone gets hurt.

463
00:20:43,024 --> 00:20:44,939
How old are these kids?

464
00:20:45,026 --> 00:20:47,115
Everyone in here's an adult.

465
00:20:47,202 --> 00:20:48,725
They're here
because they wanna be.

466
00:20:48,812 --> 00:20:51,380
Nobody's making anyone do
anything they don't wanna do.

467
00:20:51,467 --> 00:20:53,469
- You got it?
- Loud and clear.

468
00:20:53,556 --> 00:20:57,168
Did you make sure
Theissens got it, too?

469
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:59,388
Don't think you're gonna
put anything on me.

470
00:20:59,475 --> 00:21:00,998
I didn't do
anything to Wyck.

471
00:21:01,085 --> 00:21:02,783
You get to do
whatever you want

472
00:21:02,870 --> 00:21:05,002
'cause no one cares enough
to challenge it.

473
00:21:05,089 --> 00:21:07,048
But Theissens--
he didn't approve, did he?

474
00:21:07,135 --> 00:21:09,920
If he thought you were messing
with those kids of his

475
00:21:10,007 --> 00:21:11,705
he'd have happily
sent you to jail.

476
00:21:11,792 --> 00:21:14,142
You've got it
so twisted, man.

477
00:21:14,229 --> 00:21:16,797
Wyck was refusing to do
anything with any of us.

478
00:21:16,884 --> 00:21:18,233
That's what I heard.

479
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,540
But Duval said
it wasn't a problem.

480
00:21:20,627 --> 00:21:22,542
He said he'd fix it.

481
00:21:24,152 --> 00:21:26,285
Don't leave town without talking
to us first, okay?

482
00:21:33,422 --> 00:21:35,381
I could see Redgrave
murdering Theissens

483
00:21:35,468 --> 00:21:37,948
if he was afraid
to go to jail.

484
00:21:38,035 --> 00:21:39,994
Jane went to talk to Theissens'
assistants again.

485
00:21:40,081 --> 00:21:41,604
Maybe they'll give us something.

486
00:21:41,691 --> 00:21:43,650
Then again, if what
Redgrave says is true

487
00:21:43,737 --> 00:21:45,129
Duval could be our killer.

488
00:21:45,216 --> 00:21:47,349
Stay there. Watch the lobby.

489
00:21:47,436 --> 00:21:49,656
Will do.
Any sign of Mr. Liu?

490
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:52,441
A GPS on Liu's phone points
to a warehouse in Oakland.

491
00:21:52,528 --> 00:21:54,748
Cho and Rigsby
are checking it out now.

492
00:21:54,835 --> 00:22:00,667
Okay.

493
00:22:00,754 --> 00:22:02,799
Yeah. I'll call you later.

494
00:22:02,886 --> 00:22:05,672
Okay. Me, too.

495
00:22:05,759 --> 00:22:07,456
Sorry. Sarah.

496
00:22:07,543 --> 00:22:09,284
According to GPS,
he's in there.

497
00:22:09,371 --> 00:22:11,373
Okay. Let's go.

498
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:12,635
Everything okay?

499
00:22:12,722 --> 00:22:17,161
Yeah.
I mean, it's complicated.

500
00:22:17,248 --> 00:22:19,642
Sarah's pregnant.

501
00:22:19,729 --> 00:22:21,427
Oh.

502
00:22:21,514 --> 00:22:22,950
Congratulations.

503
00:22:23,037 --> 00:22:25,300
Thanks.
It's exciting, right?

504
00:22:25,387 --> 00:22:27,781
Yeah. I'm excited.

505
00:22:27,868 --> 00:22:29,348
[clatter]

506
00:22:40,794 --> 00:22:42,665
[Cho]
'Mr. Liu!
This is the CBI!'

507
00:22:42,752 --> 00:22:46,539
Nobody move!
Hands where we can see 'em.

508
00:22:46,626 --> 00:22:47,714
[coughs]

509
00:22:47,801 --> 00:22:49,629
[panting]

510
00:22:51,892 --> 00:22:54,111
There--there's no problem
here, sirs.

511
00:22:54,198 --> 00:22:57,376
We're all friends.
[panting]

512
00:22:57,463 --> 00:22:59,160
[coughs]
'No problem.'

513
00:22:59,247 --> 00:23:02,163
You can go. No problem.

514
00:23:02,250 --> 00:23:03,425
[laughs]
No problem.

515
00:23:23,750 --> 00:23:25,186
Yes? Can I help you?

516
00:23:25,273 --> 00:23:26,492
Rosalind Harker?

517
00:23:26,579 --> 00:23:28,189
Yes. Who is it?

518
00:23:28,276 --> 00:23:30,409
I'm Susan Darcy.
I'm with the FBI.

519
00:23:32,802 --> 00:23:34,761
May I come in?

520
00:23:34,848 --> 00:23:36,415
Sure.

521
00:23:42,159 --> 00:23:43,857
Miss Harker,
you recently paid a visit

522
00:23:43,944 --> 00:23:45,772
to the Sacramento County
Morgue.

523
00:23:45,859 --> 00:23:47,904
Yes.

524
00:23:47,991 --> 00:23:49,515
Did I do something wrong?
That's--

525
00:23:49,602 --> 00:23:51,168
No, it was nothing like that

526
00:23:51,255 --> 00:23:53,910
I just was wondering what
the purpose of your visit was.

527
00:23:53,997 --> 00:23:55,738
Oh.

528
00:23:55,825 --> 00:24:00,917
Well, Patrick Jane wanted me to
check if a man who was in there

529
00:24:01,004 --> 00:24:03,572
was my friend,
Roy Taglioferro.

530
00:24:03,659 --> 00:24:07,010
Roy Taglioferro,
also known as Red John?

531
00:24:07,097 --> 00:24:09,709
Mm. Well..

532
00:24:09,796 --> 00:24:13,452
that's what I've been told
by the authorities, yes.

533
00:24:13,539 --> 00:24:15,497
I suppose it must be true

534
00:24:15,584 --> 00:24:19,370
but I... still
can't quite believe it.

535
00:24:19,458 --> 00:24:21,503
I understand.

536
00:24:21,590 --> 00:24:23,723
So was it Taglioferro
in the morgue?

537
00:24:23,810 --> 00:24:26,552
No. It wasn't Roy.

538
00:24:30,643 --> 00:24:34,037
Well, thank you.
I appreciate your time.

539
00:24:34,124 --> 00:24:37,432
No, please, don't get up.
I'll see myself out.

540
00:24:37,519 --> 00:24:40,479
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

541
00:24:44,657 --> 00:24:46,310
What's your connection
to Liu?

542
00:24:46,397 --> 00:24:49,575
What went down
at the warehouse?

543
00:24:49,662 --> 00:24:52,273
No English.

544
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,188
Lawyer.

545
00:25:00,281 --> 00:25:02,501
They can lawyer up
all they want.

546
00:25:02,588 --> 00:25:05,155
All we need
is for you to testify.

547
00:25:05,242 --> 00:25:08,115
Dream on, lady.
I testify to nothing.

548
00:25:08,202 --> 00:25:10,334
You don't know these guys.

549
00:25:10,421 --> 00:25:13,163
So tell me about them.

550
00:25:13,250 --> 00:25:16,123
I import and export
to China, understand?

551
00:25:16,210 --> 00:25:20,127
I deal in electronics,
fashion, luxury goods.

552
00:25:20,214 --> 00:25:23,826
In my business, there are always
gangsters who need paying off.

553
00:25:23,913 --> 00:25:27,134
Shanghai, Guangzhou, Macau--
everywhere the same.

554
00:25:27,221 --> 00:25:28,701
What are they doing here?

555
00:25:28,788 --> 00:25:32,269
I told 'em I had no more
high-fashion copies for them.

556
00:25:32,356 --> 00:25:34,141
They came to change my mind.

557
00:25:34,228 --> 00:25:36,186
So you think they went
to Theissens first

558
00:25:36,273 --> 00:25:38,188
- to send a message to you?
- Maybe.

559
00:25:38,275 --> 00:25:40,713
If so, forget about it.

560
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:42,497
You can't touch them.

561
00:25:42,584 --> 00:25:44,325
- Really?
- Really.

562
00:25:44,412 --> 00:25:46,283
Like MC Hammer.

563
00:25:54,204 --> 00:25:56,250
Yeah, we hung out with Redgrave.

564
00:25:56,337 --> 00:25:58,165
Dude knows how to party.

565
00:25:58,252 --> 00:26:00,210
Theissens didn't like him
much, though, did he?

566
00:26:00,297 --> 00:26:02,996
Wyck? Wyck hated Redgrave.

567
00:26:03,083 --> 00:26:06,260
He represented everything that
was wrong in the fashion world,

568
00:26:06,347 --> 00:26:08,349
in Wyck's opinion.

569
00:26:08,436 --> 00:26:10,090
And he wouldn't have wanted you

570
00:26:10,177 --> 00:26:11,613
to spend time with Redgrave,
then?

571
00:26:11,700 --> 00:26:12,745
[chuckles]

572
00:26:12,832 --> 00:26:14,355
Are you kidding?

573
00:26:14,442 --> 00:26:16,052
He would have freaked.

574
00:26:16,139 --> 00:26:17,967
He was real protective of us.

575
00:26:18,054 --> 00:26:21,710
But come on. You gotta
cut loose sometimes.

576
00:26:21,797 --> 00:26:24,147
Hmm. I take it you three

577
00:26:24,234 --> 00:26:26,759
are still planning
to put the show on anyway?

578
00:26:26,846 --> 00:26:29,936
Yeah. We wanna do it
for Wyck.

579
00:26:30,023 --> 00:26:31,241
He gave us a chance.

580
00:26:31,328 --> 00:26:33,287
He taught us everything
we needed to know

581
00:26:33,374 --> 00:26:36,377
and we are gonna prove
to the world what he could do.

582
00:26:36,464 --> 00:26:38,597
Yeah, he treated us
with love and respect.

583
00:26:38,684 --> 00:26:40,468
We wanna honor him
the same way.

584
00:26:41,643 --> 00:26:44,646
Mm.

585
00:26:44,733 --> 00:26:49,564
Well, I particularly like this,
uh... gold feathery number.

586
00:26:49,651 --> 00:26:51,871
It's just so, uh...

587
00:26:51,958 --> 00:26:54,177
Well, it's an event.

588
00:26:54,264 --> 00:26:57,311
Uh, where'd you get
all these gold feathers?

589
00:26:57,398 --> 00:26:59,182
We dyed them.

590
00:26:59,269 --> 00:27:02,359
Combination of henna
and iron oxide or something.

591
00:27:02,446 --> 00:27:04,100
Tristan was gonna model it

592
00:27:04,187 --> 00:27:07,234
and Wyck was gonna
close the show with it.

593
00:27:07,321 --> 00:27:09,497
Do you have any more
of those feathers?

594
00:27:09,584 --> 00:27:11,978
I guess so... if you want.

595
00:27:24,860 --> 00:27:26,427
Why the long faces?

596
00:27:26,514 --> 00:27:28,734
You see those two over there
talking to Wainright?

597
00:27:28,821 --> 00:27:31,650
The one with the red tie
looks like state department.

598
00:27:31,737 --> 00:27:33,173
He is.

599
00:27:33,260 --> 00:27:35,262
The other one's from
the Chinese embassy.

600
00:27:35,349 --> 00:27:37,394
Apparently the three
that were intimidating Liu

601
00:27:37,481 --> 00:27:38,613
have diplomatic immunity.

602
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:40,180
Wainright's cutting 'em loose.

603
00:27:40,267 --> 00:27:43,139
Well, I'd best go
talk to them right away.

604
00:27:43,226 --> 00:27:44,967
Agent Darcy. Hi.

605
00:27:45,054 --> 00:27:48,188
I need to talk
to you, please. May I ?

606
00:27:48,275 --> 00:27:49,493
[both]
Of course.

607
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:51,234
Is there somewhere
we can talk?

608
00:27:51,321 --> 00:27:53,846
I just need to do one thing.
Where are those gangsters?

609
00:27:53,933 --> 00:27:56,631
In the interrogation room
with their lawyer.

610
00:27:56,718 --> 00:27:58,677
- Come on.
- Thanks.

611
00:28:04,639 --> 00:28:06,902
This won't take a minute.

612
00:28:30,752 --> 00:28:32,101
What was that all about?

613
00:28:32,188 --> 00:28:34,669
-Just trying to solve a murder.

614
00:28:34,756 --> 00:28:35,888
- Tea?
- No, thank you.

615
00:28:35,975 --> 00:28:37,672
I just have
a couple of questions

616
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:39,805
I need you to clarify for me.

617
00:28:39,892 --> 00:28:42,764
Oh. Fire away.

618
00:28:42,851 --> 00:28:44,810
[water running]

619
00:28:44,897 --> 00:28:47,421
Rosalind Harker.

620
00:28:48,814 --> 00:28:50,729
You met her a couple of
years ago

621
00:28:50,816 --> 00:28:52,252
when you were
tracking Red John?

622
00:28:52,339 --> 00:28:54,297
Uh, yes.

623
00:28:54,384 --> 00:28:56,865
That's correct.

624
00:28:56,952 --> 00:28:58,562
Why do you ask?

625
00:28:58,649 --> 00:29:00,434
She was the lover of a man--

626
00:29:00,521 --> 00:29:02,566
Roy Taglioferro?

627
00:29:02,653 --> 00:29:04,351
Right. Who was really
Red John?

628
00:29:04,438 --> 00:29:06,701
Yes.

629
00:29:06,788 --> 00:29:08,485
But you took Rosalind
to the morgue

630
00:29:08,572 --> 00:29:10,531
to look at the body
of Timothy Carter--

631
00:29:10,618 --> 00:29:13,055
Timothy Carter, who you killed
because hewas Red John.

632
00:29:13,142 --> 00:29:14,796
Yes.

633
00:29:16,929 --> 00:29:18,713
Rosalind told you
that Timothy Carter

634
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:20,584
wasn't Taglioferro,
didn't she?

635
00:29:20,671 --> 00:29:23,587
Yes. I was hoping
for confirmation from her.

636
00:29:23,674 --> 00:29:25,851
She's hardly
a rock-solid witness.

637
00:29:25,938 --> 00:29:28,157
It had been many years
since her last contact

638
00:29:28,244 --> 00:29:30,029
with Mr. Taglioferro.

639
00:29:30,116 --> 00:29:32,509
She's kind of a lonely soul.

640
00:29:32,596 --> 00:29:33,859
I think she'd rather believe

641
00:29:33,946 --> 00:29:36,165
he was still out there
alive somewhere.

642
00:29:36,252 --> 00:29:39,125
Hmm.

643
00:29:39,212 --> 00:29:41,127
I suppose you're right.

644
00:29:41,214 --> 00:29:43,216
It was Red John
that I killed.

645
00:29:44,826 --> 00:29:46,436
I sure hope so.

646
00:29:50,963 --> 00:29:52,660
Thanks, Patrick.

647
00:29:52,747 --> 00:29:54,531
Pleasure.

648
00:30:03,889 --> 00:30:05,804
I checked out the Chinese thugs.
They're clean.

649
00:30:05,891 --> 00:30:07,631
Let's go to the hotel,
shall we?

650
00:30:07,718 --> 00:30:09,764
Uh, aside from the kids
helping Theissens

651
00:30:09,851 --> 00:30:11,853
only the killer
knows what this is.

652
00:30:11,940 --> 00:30:13,550
I'll tell Rigsby and Van Pelt.

653
00:30:17,163 --> 00:30:18,599
Tell me what happened
with Darcy.

654
00:30:18,686 --> 00:30:20,514
I know it was something.

655
00:30:20,601 --> 00:30:22,298
Well, it's nothing important.

656
00:30:23,734 --> 00:30:25,258
It's bad news.

657
00:30:25,345 --> 00:30:27,738
You've got a bad news expression
on your face.

658
00:30:29,392 --> 00:30:32,221
Darcy talked
to Rosalind Harker.

659
00:30:32,308 --> 00:30:34,615
She knows Timothy Carter
wasn't Red John.

660
00:30:34,702 --> 00:30:37,139
Well, she might suspect,
but she doesn't know.

661
00:30:37,226 --> 00:30:38,880
And you're not
gonna tell her?

662
00:30:38,967 --> 00:30:42,101
Well, of course not.
Why stir up trouble?

663
00:30:44,712 --> 00:30:45,800
Hmm?

664
00:30:47,367 --> 00:30:48,629
Let's go.

665
00:30:57,943 --> 00:30:59,640
Hey, we're headed over
to the hotel.

666
00:30:59,727 --> 00:31:01,468
You on top
of everything here?

667
00:31:01,555 --> 00:31:02,904
Hmm?

668
00:31:02,991 --> 00:31:05,646
Oh, yeah.
Sure.

669
00:31:07,735 --> 00:31:10,999
Wayne?
You're reading a baby book.

670
00:31:11,086 --> 00:31:13,784
Um, yeah, I am.

671
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:16,526
Um, why?

672
00:31:16,613 --> 00:31:18,224
I...

673
00:31:18,311 --> 00:31:19,225
Yes.

674
00:31:20,791 --> 00:31:23,055
I'm pregnant.

675
00:31:23,142 --> 00:31:24,404
Sarah's pregnant.

676
00:31:25,927 --> 00:31:27,886
- I'm having a baby.
- Oh, my god.

677
00:31:27,973 --> 00:31:30,279
Yikes.

678
00:31:30,366 --> 00:31:32,194
I mean...
Sorry.

679
00:31:32,281 --> 00:31:34,805
It surprised me.
Congratulations.

680
00:31:34,893 --> 00:31:37,460
No, it was a surprise
to me, too.

681
00:31:37,547 --> 00:31:39,375
Still is, actually.

682
00:31:39,462 --> 00:31:43,031
Hard even for me
to believe sometimes.

683
00:31:43,118 --> 00:31:44,685
Are you okay?

684
00:31:44,772 --> 00:31:47,818
Yeah. Oh, I'm--
babies are good, right?

685
00:31:49,342 --> 00:31:50,691
Always wanted to have kids.

686
00:31:50,778 --> 00:31:54,608
Just a little earlier
than I expected.

687
00:31:54,695 --> 00:31:56,392
So are you and Sarah
getting married?

688
00:31:56,479 --> 00:31:59,004
Oh, no. No.
Nothing like that.

689
00:31:59,091 --> 00:32:01,920
Don't wanna rush
into anything, right?

690
00:32:03,573 --> 00:32:06,141
Haven't even been dating
that long.

691
00:32:08,622 --> 00:32:11,538
If... you need anything,
you can ask.

692
00:32:11,625 --> 00:32:13,235
You know that, right?

693
00:32:13,322 --> 00:32:16,804
Yeah.
You should get going, though.

694
00:32:16,891 --> 00:32:18,371
Yeah.

695
00:32:21,287 --> 00:32:23,985
Uh, Wayne..

696
00:32:24,072 --> 00:32:26,683
The kid's lucky.
You're gonna make a great dad.

697
00:32:26,770 --> 00:32:28,511
Yeah? You think?

698
00:32:28,598 --> 00:32:31,340
Yeah. I know it.

699
00:32:31,427 --> 00:32:32,689
Bye.

700
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:38,086
Thanks.

701
00:32:41,350 --> 00:32:44,223
[indistinct conversations]

702
00:32:48,575 --> 00:32:50,055
Mr. Duval. Hi.

703
00:32:50,142 --> 00:32:52,709
We just need to clear
a few things up.

704
00:32:52,796 --> 00:32:54,189
This is approaching harassment.

705
00:32:54,276 --> 00:32:55,799
We have spoken
to our lawyers.

706
00:32:55,886 --> 00:32:57,236
- Come with me, please.
- Why?

707
00:32:57,323 --> 00:32:59,542
I have a question
I'd like to ask you.

708
00:32:59,629 --> 00:33:01,240
What kind of question?

709
00:33:01,327 --> 00:33:03,764
It's the kind of question
that could clear your name

710
00:33:03,851 --> 00:33:06,201
or prove your guilt.
But, uh, first of all

711
00:33:06,288 --> 00:33:10,684
I'd like you to
empty your pockets, please.

712
00:33:10,771 --> 00:33:11,902
This is ridiculous.

713
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:13,121
Please.

714
00:33:15,471 --> 00:33:16,820
[sighs]

715
00:33:23,218 --> 00:33:24,654
what is this?

716
00:33:27,744 --> 00:33:29,877
What does it look like?

717
00:33:29,964 --> 00:33:33,141
Well, it's obviously a feather.
It's not mine.

718
00:33:34,403 --> 00:33:36,927
Where did this come from?

719
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,929
Lisbon,
our work here is done.

720
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:43,369
Thank you for your time,
Mr. Duval. Mrs. Duval.

721
00:33:43,456 --> 00:33:46,676
[both speaking French]

722
00:33:57,252 --> 00:33:59,385
- Hey, Junior.
- Hey. What's up?

723
00:33:59,472 --> 00:34:01,256
How's your investigation going?

724
00:34:01,343 --> 00:34:04,564
Well, that's why we're here.
I found the killer.

725
00:34:04,651 --> 00:34:05,956
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

726
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,871
Well, who is it?
What happened?

727
00:34:09,873 --> 00:34:12,485
The clue was right
in front of my eyes.

728
00:34:12,572 --> 00:34:15,401
It's all here
in this magazine.

729
00:34:15,488 --> 00:34:17,925
Whoa.

730
00:34:18,012 --> 00:34:21,972
That's... pretty cool.
Is it yours?

731
00:34:22,799 --> 00:34:25,846
Hmm.

732
00:34:25,933 --> 00:34:28,153
Hey, what article
am I supposed to be reading?

733
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:30,894
Thank you for your time,
Mr. Acosta. We'll stay in touch.

734
00:34:35,334 --> 00:34:36,987
Yes. I love that.

735
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,554
[knock on door]

736
00:34:38,641 --> 00:34:40,382
Don't move a muscle.

737
00:34:43,472 --> 00:34:44,386
Yes?

738
00:34:44,473 --> 00:34:46,258
Hello.

739
00:34:46,345 --> 00:34:48,390
Hi. I'm agent Teresa Lisbon.

740
00:34:48,477 --> 00:34:50,218
You've already met
Patrick Jane, right?

741
00:34:50,305 --> 00:34:51,872
- Hey.
- Hi.

742
00:34:51,959 --> 00:34:54,179
What do you want?
You come to hassle me

743
00:34:54,266 --> 00:34:56,529
about Wyck Theissens' death
some more, have you?

744
00:34:56,616 --> 00:34:59,097
Not really. One or two more
things falling into place

745
00:34:59,184 --> 00:35:00,620
and the killer
shall be revealed.

746
00:35:00,707 --> 00:35:01,882
[knock on door]

747
00:35:01,969 --> 00:35:02,970
I'll get it.

748
00:35:05,538 --> 00:35:08,628
So why have you come here?

749
00:35:08,715 --> 00:35:13,372
I need your help.

750
00:35:13,459 --> 00:35:15,765
hey. I didn't order
room service.

751
00:35:15,852 --> 00:35:17,071
Where did that come from?

752
00:35:17,158 --> 00:35:19,117
Oh, all I know
is that I'm starving.

753
00:35:19,204 --> 00:35:22,163
Do you think I could, uh,
have something from here?

754
00:35:26,863 --> 00:35:28,822
What the hell is that?

755
00:35:28,909 --> 00:35:32,304
It means nothing to you?

756
00:35:32,391 --> 00:35:34,262
Why would it?

757
00:35:40,877 --> 00:35:42,966
You.

758
00:35:45,012 --> 00:35:46,231
Ma'am!

759
00:35:47,580 --> 00:35:49,364
Ma'am! Stop!

760
00:35:49,451 --> 00:35:51,279
I got her.

761
00:35:51,366 --> 00:35:53,890
You're under arrest.

762
00:35:53,977 --> 00:35:55,414
You're losing your touch.

763
00:35:55,501 --> 00:35:56,937
You didn't know it was her.

764
00:35:57,024 --> 00:35:58,199
Don't be ridiculous.

765
00:35:58,286 --> 00:36:00,549
The trick worked
exactly as I intended.

766
00:36:00,636 --> 00:36:03,204
It didn't matter which one
I thought it was.

767
00:36:03,291 --> 00:36:06,076
That's how
a good trick works.

768
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,341
You wouldsay that,
wouldn't you?

769
00:36:09,428 --> 00:36:11,865
[clicks]

770
00:36:21,788 --> 00:36:24,356
We've got your fingerprints
on the murder weapon, Sasha.

771
00:36:24,443 --> 00:36:26,923
It's a perfect match.

772
00:36:27,010 --> 00:36:28,360
Tell me what happened.

773
00:36:30,753 --> 00:36:33,234
It was supposed to be me.

774
00:36:33,321 --> 00:36:37,107
I was supposed to be the face
of Wyck's return.

775
00:36:37,195 --> 00:36:40,720
Because you had been
his inspiration before?

776
00:36:40,807 --> 00:36:43,810
That's right.
I was his muse.

777
00:36:43,897 --> 00:36:46,073
So you went to talk to him
that night?

778
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:48,684
Mm-hmm.

779
00:36:48,771 --> 00:36:52,035
He was nice, but distant.

780
00:36:52,122 --> 00:36:53,950
I wanted to see the clothes

781
00:36:54,037 --> 00:36:56,562
and he didn't want
to show me them.

782
00:36:56,649 --> 00:36:59,260
I should've known then.

783
00:36:59,347 --> 00:37:01,828
'I told him
they were all beautiful.'

784
00:37:01,915 --> 00:37:04,700
'But there was
this golden feather dress'

785
00:37:04,787 --> 00:37:06,528
'that just hooked me.'

786
00:37:06,615 --> 00:37:08,443
'And that's when he told me.'

787
00:37:08,530 --> 00:37:12,447
'He told me he had found
someone new and fresh.'

788
00:37:12,534 --> 00:37:14,884
'Some little bitch
named Tristan.'

789
00:37:14,971 --> 00:37:18,192
'He told me I was too old.'

790
00:37:18,279 --> 00:37:21,195
'You must have felt
angry, betrayed, even.'

791
00:37:21,282 --> 00:37:23,719
'How could he think he could
treat me like that?'

792
00:37:23,806 --> 00:37:27,201
'So I wanted
to make him suffer.'

793
00:37:27,288 --> 00:37:30,509
'I wanted to make him
eat those words.'

794
00:37:34,426 --> 00:37:36,645
So am I gonna be
outta here soon?

795
00:37:36,732 --> 00:37:38,691
I have a show
in a couple hours

796
00:37:38,778 --> 00:37:42,347
and I need to get there early
for makeup and fitting.

797
00:37:42,434 --> 00:37:43,348
No.

798
00:37:45,306 --> 00:37:48,178
You're not going
to be in the show.

799
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,267
No more shows.

800
00:37:49,354 --> 00:37:53,967
[cell phone rings]

801
00:37:54,054 --> 00:37:55,925
Hello? This is Patrick.

802
00:37:56,012 --> 00:38:00,321
[Rosalind]
'This is Rosalind Harker.
Roy came to see me.'

803
00:38:02,802 --> 00:38:04,673
Is he still there, Rosalind?

804
00:38:04,760 --> 00:38:07,502
'Yes, Roy's here.'

805
00:38:07,589 --> 00:38:10,244
Like I thought, it's all
a big misunderstanding.

806
00:38:10,331 --> 00:38:13,769
He says to tell you
and that Darcy woman

807
00:38:13,856 --> 00:38:15,554
he's going
to clear it all up.

808
00:38:15,641 --> 00:38:18,774
Okay.
Uh, and you're at home?

809
00:38:18,861 --> 00:38:20,950
[laughs]
Where else would I be?

810
00:38:21,037 --> 00:38:23,083
And you're okay?

811
00:38:23,170 --> 00:38:24,737
Of course I am.

812
00:38:24,824 --> 00:38:27,566
Okay. I-I'm on my way.

813
00:38:29,785 --> 00:38:31,221
I want teams around back.

814
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:33,398
Set up a perimeter.
Nobody in or out.

815
00:38:33,485 --> 00:38:35,008
[piano music]

816
00:39:19,879 --> 00:39:24,013
Rosalind. Where's Roy?

817
00:39:24,100 --> 00:39:26,102
Roy couldn't stay.

818
00:39:28,061 --> 00:39:29,410
Jane

819
00:39:29,497 --> 00:39:32,370
[music continues]

820
00:39:57,090 --> 00:39:59,309
It's the morgue attendant.

821
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:09,015
You still gonna try
and tell me Red John is dead?

822
00:40:13,628 --> 00:40:16,109
[music continues]

